	(text "Source: hardware/power-analysis.md (2026-10-27) and Power Arch. 2026-10-27.drawio.png. Module-level wiring schematic:\nPololu, Adafruit, DFRobot and Luxonis parts are off-the-shelf boards; footprints are left blank on purpose.\n\nRAILS\n  VPACK      pack + (BT1) to F1                        10.6-16.8 V\n  VBAT_F     after F1; charge diode U1 lands here so charging works with SW1 off\n  +VBAT      switched bus after SW1, D2 TVS clamps spikes (SMBJ18CA, 29 V clamp < 36 V INA260 limit)\n  VMOT_SW / VMOT   motor branch after K1 and after U2 shunt; C1 bulk at DFR0601 P+\n  +5V_COMP   Buck A (U5) -> Raspberry Pi 5 only. U4 ideal diode + C2 isolate it from motor sag\n  +5V_SENS   Buck B (U7) -> OAK, D500, ESP32, DFR0601 logic, encoders, K2, RC RX, LEDs\n  +3V3       ESP32 board LDO -> INA260 ×3 VCC, VL53L4CD ×4 VIN (keeps I2C at 3.3 V for the ESP32)\n\nCURRENT SENSE (INA260, 2 mΩ internal, high side)\n  U2 0x40 motor (A0/A1 open) · U3 0x41 compute (A0 -> VS) · U6 0x44 sensor (A1 -> VS). I2C master: ESP32 IO21/IO22.\n  INA260 VCC = 3V3, so the breakout pull-ups go to 3.3 V. ALERT unused; VBUS jumpered to VIN- on the breakout.\n\nFUSING\n  F1 10 A main (ATO slow): wiring short-circuit protection. Normal peak 2.8 A @14.4 V; capped stall 9.2 A.\n  F2 / F3 3 A per buck branch: buck input <= 1.2 A at 10.6 V and 11-12 W out, plus C2/C3 inrush.\n  F4 0.5 A on the K1 coil chain (142 mA max at 16.8 V).\n\nMOTOR ENABLE (spec: power-analysis §2.3 #14, firmware e-stop interlock)\n  K1 coil = +VBAT -> F4 -> SW2 E-stop (NC) -> K2 RC relay (NO) -> R1 15 Ω -> coil -> Q1 (ESP32 MOTOR_EN).\n  Any one of the three opens K1 and removes motor power; RC loss de-energises K2 (fail-safe).\n\nOPEN ITEMS / CHECK BEFORE BUILD\n  1. D36V50F5 is 5.0 V ±4 %: the Pi 5 wants 5.1 V. Check for under-voltage warnings under load; add\n     usb_max_current_enable=1 only if the Pi USB load stays well under the buck's budget.\n  2. Pack chemistry/size not final: re-check F1 against the chosen pack's BMS limit.\n  3. Confirm #2804 relay fail-safe behaviour on RC signal loss on the bench.\n  4. Validate every figure with the three INA260 readings (power-analysis header).\n  5. Control signals (DFR0601 PWM/IN, encoder A/B, VL53 XSHUT, LiDAR UART) belong on a control sheet.\n  6. K2 OUT (high = relay energised) and GOOD (valid RC signal) are spare: wire to the ESP32 to monitor the enable chain.\n\nMANUFACTURER DOCUMENTS: hardware/datasheets/KiCAD (index in hardware/datasheets/README). Every symbol's Datasheet field opens the local\ncopy; Schematic / Pinout / Drawing fields point to the manufacturer board schematic where one is published.\nNot published: D36V50F5, Raspberry Pi 5, Camera Module 3, OAK-D Pro W, D500 LiDAR (module datasheets linked instead)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
